<title>QATAR: Qatargas to sell spot LNG cargoes in Europe.</title>
<headline>Qatargas to sell spot LNG cargoes in Europe.</headline>
<dateline>DOHA 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Qatargas will sell spot cargoes of liquefied natural gas (LNG) in Europe this September, Qatar Energy and Industry Minister Abdullah bin Hamad al-Attiyah said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The sales from the Qatargas project to Europe would be a marketing breakthrough for the new company which, since its first export cargo in December, has focused on Japanese markets.</p>
<p>&quot;I am optimistic that Qatargas will have a share in the European market in the future,&quot; he said. Attiyah would not disclose where the cargoes would be sold in Europe.</p>
<p>Qatargas is a joint venture between state-owned Qatar General Petroleum Corp, the United States Mobil Corp, Total of France and Japanese trading companies Mitsui and Marubeni.</p>
</text>
